---
functor: 1
title: slant
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`slant` · deform · lean to the right, a slanted variant.

# Form

`x.slant` on a symbol, `(a + b).slant` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `A.slant` | $A.slant$ | built and cached |
| `x.slant` | $x.slant$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | Lean to the right, a slanted variant. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A changed outline of the base. The compiler moves each point of the outline, and the strokes keep their shape and width. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- Leans the base 12 degrees to the right. The width stays the same.

# From LaTeX

`\textsl` and slanted fonts, for one symbol.

